## Summary

Market Stage: Early (Post-TGE, Mainnet Live < 6 Months, Limited Public Metrics)
Primary Category: Data Liquidity / Data DAO Infrastructure
Competitor Count: 8+ identified (Ocean, Streamr, Ceramic, Filecoin, Arweave, Sahara AI, Masa, DIMO)
Major Narrative: Data DAO / Data Liquidity (Main); Data Sovereignty (Main); AI Training Data (Secondary); Modular App-Chain (Secondary); EVM-Compatible L1 (Secondary)
Trading Availability: CEX (multiple, names undisclosed), DEX (Vana L1 + Ethereum via bridge), Price Tracking (CoinGecko, CoinMarketCap)
Adoption Metrics Available: Minimal — only Data DAO count (5) verified; TVL, users, transactions, volume, staking metrics not publicly aggregated

## Open Threads

- Specific CEX listing venues, trading pairs, and listing dates for VANA token — not publicly announced
- Market maker / liquidity provider arrangements for VANA — not disclosed
- 24h/7d/30d trading volume history (CEX + DEX aggregated) — not available from single verified source
- TVL at protocol level and per Data DAO — no public dashboard; Vana not on DeFiLlama
- Daily/Monthly Active Users (unique addresses transacting) — no public analytics
- Total staked VANA, staking ratio, validator count, Nakamoto coefficient — explorer shows raw data only
- Bridge volume (Vana-Ethereum) historical — no public analytics
- Developer activity metrics (commits, active devs, repos) — GitHub raw data only, not aggregated
- Market share vs. competitors (Ocean, Streamr, etc.) — category not tracked by analytics platforms
- VANA token circulating supply, FDV, market cap (current) — CoinGecko shows but not cross-verified with on-chain
- Holder distribution (whale concentration, foundation %, investor %, community %) — not disclosed
- Unlock schedule impact on liquidity (vesting cliffs for team/investors) — not public
- Grant program deployment and ecosystem funding metrics — referenced in whitepaper, no public data
- Audit status and any security incidents — none announced
- Regulatory status in key jurisdictions (US, EU) for Data DAO model — whitepaper acknowledges uncertainty
- Enterprise partnerships beyond 5 Data DAOs — not documented
- IBC active channels, relayer status, cross-chain volume — enabled but not documented
- Whether Moksha testnet incentives/state migrated to mainnet — not documented
- Fee switch / protocol revenue activation status — whitepaper mentions, not confirmed live
- Treasury size, composition, runway — not disclosed